# Dashboard

Vite + React + TypeScript + Tailwind + Recharts. Five views over one `ScanContext`, which owns
the selected scan, health, job status, and polling. Import through the `@/` alias.

## Data

- New data means extending `lib/api.ts` and mirroring the Pydantic model in `lib/types.ts`.
- Anything a stored older scan will not have must be optional in the type and handled as absent
  in the view. The Trends page reads history, so a field assumed present breaks it.
- Distinguish absent from unmeasured on screen: an unpriced resource shows as unpriced, never as
  `$0`. Formatting `null` is `lib/format.ts`'s job — use `money`, `percent`, `bytes`,
  `metricValue`, not inline `toFixed`.
- Metric keys are matched by pattern in `metricValue` to decide the unit, so name derived metrics
  consistently with the existing keys.

## Components

Build from the primitives in `components/ui.tsx` — `Card`, `Badge`, `cx`, the table and empty
states — rather than fresh markup, and from `components/charts.tsx` for Recharts wrappers.
Tailwind uses the project's semantic tokens (`ink`, `line`, `surface`, `good`, `warn`, `bad`,
`accent`); do not introduce raw palette colours.

## Presentation is not accounting

Grouping in the Savings table is display only. Totals come from the findings as the backend sent
them, so a grouped row shows the sum of its members and never replaces them.

## Checks

`npx tsc --noEmit` must pass, and `npm run build` before `finops serve` shows anything. Never run
Prettier ad hoc — it rewraps at 80 columns and fights the existing style.
